course: dictionary
lesson: 3768
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Fold» is one of these words. It can be an action (to fold something) or a thing (a fold).
explain: To fold is to bend paper or cloth so one part lies over another. «She folded her arms» means she crossed them over her chest. Fold your arms, and you are doing the action; a fold is the line or crease that the bending leaves behind.
explain: Use the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence and check it makes sense. In «The sensitive plant folds its leaflets within seconds when touched», folds means bends its leaves together. A pen for sheep would not make sense there, so that meaning is wrong.
fact: Fold is a verb and a noun: you can fold paper, or look at the fold it leaves.
fact: «Fold in half» means bend something so one half lies over the other.
fact: «Threefold» means three times as much. The ending «-fold» tells you how many times.
fact: «Origami» is the art of folding paper into shapes.
fact: «The shop folded» means the business closed. A fold can also be a pen for sheep, so always check the context.
exercise: «Fold the paper in half, then fold it again.» What does fold mean here? | a line of symmetry | a pen for sheep | *bend so one part lies over another | close a business
exercise: «The fold of belly skin kept the chick warm.» What is a fold in this sentence? | a pen for sheep | to bend something | *a crease or flap of skin | a closed business
exercise: «The shop folded last year.» What does folded mean? | It was bent in half | It was packed away for storage | It was folded up neatly | *It closed for business
test: What does «threefold» mean? | three sides | *three times as much | a line of three creases | a pen for three sheep
test: «A tube folded up in your belly.» What does folded up mean? | dropped quickly | pushed out of the body | *bent over and packed into a small space | opened wide
exam: «She folded her arms and said nothing.» What does folded mean? | a line on paper | a pen for sheep | closed the business | *crossed them over her chest
